1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:03,550
Every number carries a clue about its divisors. Here

2
00:00:03,550 --> 00:00:07,058
are the quick tests for six divisors, with no

3
00:00:07,058 --> 00:00:10,331
long division at all. Look, add, combine.

4
00:00:10,987 --> 00:00:14,680
Hasini has one hundred and twenty five chocolates to

5
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:17,027
share. Traders shared grain this way for centuries. Five

6
00:00:17,027 --> 00:00:19,857
at a time gives twenty five groups; six leaves

7
00:00:19,857 --> 00:00:23,557
five over. Every guess costs a division. So can

8
00:00:23,557 --> 00:00:26,918
we tell without dividing? Yes, with a divisibility rule.

9
00:00:27,407 --> 00:00:30,850
What does divisible mean? Twenty four divided by four

10
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:34,747
is six equal groups, remainder zero. Twenty nine leaves

11
00:00:34,747 --> 00:00:39,147
one over. Remainder zero: that is the test. Now

12
00:00:39,147 --> 00:00:40,758
inspect the digits.

13
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:45,580
Divisibility by two. Take nine hundred fifty three and

14
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:49,160
nine thousand five hundred thirty four. Only the ones

15
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:53,720
digit matters. Even endings: zero, two, four, six, eight.

16
00:00:53,720 --> 00:01:00,111
The second passes; the first does not. Ignore every other digit.

17
00:01:00,587 --> 00:01:04,307
Divisibility by five and ten. Five thousand seven hundred

18
00:01:04,307 --> 00:01:07,879
eighty five ends in five: five divides it. One

19
00:01:07,879 --> 00:01:10,930
thousand two hundred fifty ends in zero: five and

20
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:14,987
ten divide it. Two needs even; five needs zero

21
00:01:14,987 --> 00:01:18,238
or five; ten needs zero. Three rules, one glance.

22
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:22,682
Divisibility by three is different. Twenty seven and thirty

23
00:01:22,682 --> 00:01:25,248
seven both end in seven, yet only twenty seven

24
00:01:25,248 --> 00:01:28,771
divides by three. Add the digits of thirty six

25
00:01:28,771 --> 00:01:32,453
thousand one hundred twenty nine. Three, six, one, two,

26
00:01:32,453 --> 00:01:36,531
nine: twenty one, which three divides. So the number does too.

27
00:01:37,153 --> 00:01:41,993
Divisibility by nine: the same digits, a stronger question.

28
00:01:41,993 --> 00:01:45,213
Nine thousand eight hundred forty six. Nine, eight, four,

29
00:01:45,213 --> 00:01:49,043
six: twenty seven, which is nine times three. So

30
00:01:49,043 --> 00:01:53,584
nine divides it. Same digits, stronger question.

31
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:58,419
Divisibility by six needs two tests. Seven thousand two

32
00:01:58,419 --> 00:02:02,150
hundred twenty four ends in four, an even digit.

33
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:07,660
Seven, two, two, four: fifteen, and three divides fifteen.

34
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:11,561
Both pass, so six divides it. Remember the word both.

35
00:02:12,191 --> 00:02:16,171
Now use it. Three hundred seventy two runners want

36
00:02:16,171 --> 00:02:21,251
equal teams of six. Test two: the number ends

37
00:02:21,251 --> 00:02:24,891
in two. Test three: three, seven, two, twelve. Both

38
00:02:24,891 --> 00:02:27,222
pass: sixty two teams, nobody out.

39
00:02:27,844 --> 00:02:30,464
Which of two, three, five, six, nine and ten

40
00:02:30,464 --> 00:02:33,504
divide twelve thousand three hundred forty five? Pause and

41
00:02:33,504 --> 00:02:37,984
decide. The last digit is five, which is odd:

42
00:02:37,984 --> 00:02:42,284
two fails, and six too. Five passes, and ten

43
00:02:42,284 --> 00:02:46,674
fails. The digits add to fifteen: three passes, nine

44
00:02:46,674 --> 00:02:49,815
fails. Divisible by three and five.

45
00:02:50,456 --> 00:02:54,546
All six rules, in three ideas. Last digit: two

46
00:02:54,546 --> 00:02:57,236
needs even; five needs zero or five; ten needs

47
00:02:57,236 --> 00:03:00,960
zero. Add the digits: three needs a sum divisible

48
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:04,036
by three; nine by nine. Combine: six needs two

49
00:03:04,036 --> 00:03:08,176
and three together. Look, add, combine. Thank you for

50
00:03:08,176 --> 00:03:10,267
watching. See you next lesson.
